\textbf{Build the matrix row by row.}

For each row $v_i$: put a \textbf{1} in column $v_j$ if there is a
directed edge $v_i \to v_j$ (or a loop if $i=j$).

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|c|l|l|}
\hline
\rowcolor{primaryblue!20}
\textbf{Row} & \textbf{Outgoing edges from this vertex} &
\textbf{Row entries} \\
\hline
$a$ & Loop at $a$; edges to $b$, $c$, $d$ &
    $[1,\;1,\;1,\;1]$ \\
\hline
$b$ & Edges to $a$, $d$ &
    $[1,\;0,\;0,\;1]$ \\
\hline
$c$ & Edges to $a$, $d$ &
    $[1,\;0,\;0,\;1]$ \\
\hline
$d$ & Edges to $b$, $c$ (not to $a$) &
    $[0,\;1,\;1,\;0]$ \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
