\textbf{Step 3 --- Structure:}

In $G_1$: vertices 1 and 4 (both degree 3) are \textbf{directly
adjacent} via edge $(1,4)$.

In $G_2$: vertices $a$ and $e$ (both degree 3) are \textbf{directly
adjacent} via edge $(a,e)$. Structure matches.

\textbf{Step 4 --- Build bijection:}

Match degree-3 vertices: $f(1)=a$, $\; f(4)=e$.

Neighbours of $1$ in $G_1$: $\{2,\,6,\,4\}$.
Neighbours of $a$ in $G_2$: $\{b,\,c,\,e\}$.

Already placed $f(4)=e$. Assign $f(2)=b$, $f(6)=c$.

Neighbours of $4$ in $G_1$: $\{1,\,3,\,5\}$.
Neighbours of $e$ in $G_2$: $\{a,\,d,\,f\}$.

Already placed $f(1)=a$. Assign $f(3)=d$, $f(5)=f$.

\textbf{Bijection:}
\[
f:\quad 1\mapsto a,\;\; 2\mapsto b,\;\; 3\mapsto d,\;\;
        4\mapsto e,\;\; 5\mapsto f,\;\; 6\mapsto c
\]

\textbf{Step 5 --- Verify all 7 edges:}

\begin{center}
