\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

This assignment fails at edge $(2,3)$. Retry with $f(2)=b$ but
swap $f(3)$ and $f(5)$. Looking more carefully at $G_2$:
the path $a$--$b$--$f$--$e$ suggests $b$ connects to $f$, not $d$.

Try: $f(1)=a,\; f(2)=b,\; f(3)=f,\; f(4)=e,\; f(5)=d,\; f(6)=c$.

\textbf{Re-verify all 7 edges:}

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|}
\hline
\rowcolor{primaryblue!20}
\textbf{Edge in $G_1$} & \textbf{Image under $f$} &
\textbf{In $E(G_2)$?} \\
\hline
$(1,2)$ & $(a,b)$ & \textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark} \\
$(2,3)$ & $(b,f)$ & \textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark} \\
$(3,4)$ & $(f,e)$ & \textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark} \\
$(4,5)$ & $(e,d)$ & \textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark} \\
$(5,6)$ & $(d,c)$ & \textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark} \\
$(6,1)$ & $(c,a)$ & \textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark} \\
$(1,4)$ & $(a,e)$ & \textcolor{darkgreen}{\checkmark} \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

All 7 edges verified.
\[
\boxed{G_1 \cong G_2 \text{ via }
f: 1\mapsto a,\;2\mapsto b,\;3\mapsto f,\;
   4\mapsto e,\;5\mapsto d,\;6\mapsto c}
\]

\textit{Note: It is normal to need more than one attempt. Always
verify \textbf{every} edge before concluding isomorphism.}

