\vspace{0.6cm}

If $G$ is a simple graph with $n \geq 3$ vertices and for every pair
of \textbf{non-adjacent} vertices $u, v$:
\[
    \deg(u) + \deg(v) \;\geq\; n
\]
then $G$ has a \textbf{Hamiltonian circuit}.

\vspace{0.3cm}
\textbf{Relationship:} Dirac's theorem is a special case of Ore's.
If $\deg(v)\geq n/2$ for all $v$, then any two non-adjacent
vertices satisfy $\deg(u)+\deg(v)\geq n/2+n/2=n$.

