\vspace{0.5cm}

Every \textbf{planar graph} can be properly vertex-colored
with at most \textbf{4 colors}:
\[
    G \text{ planar} \;\implies\; \chi(G) \leq 4
\]

\vspace{0.2cm}
\textbf{History:} Conjectured 1852 by Francis Guthrie;
proved 1976 by Appel and Haken --- the first major theorem
proved with computer assistance (verified 1936 unavoidable
configurations).

