Considers \textbf{all edges globally}, sorted cheapest first.
Adds each edge only if it \textbf{does not create a cycle}.

\vspace{0.25cm}
\textcolor{primaryblue}{\textbf{Steps:}}
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=2em, topsep=2pt, itemsep=1pt]
  \item Sort all edges in non-decreasing weight order.
  \item Set $T=\emptyset$.
  \item For each edge in order: add it to $T$ if its two
        endpoints are in \textbf{different components};
        otherwise skip.
  \item Stop when $T$ has $n-1$ edges.
\end{enumerate}

\vspace{0.2cm}
$T$ may be a disconnected forest during construction.
Components merge until one connected subgraph remains.

