\vspace{0.8cm}

Finds the \textbf{shortest path from source $s$} to all other
vertices. Requires \textbf{non-negative} edge weights.

\vspace{0.25cm}
\textcolor{primaryblue}{\textbf{Steps:}}
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=2em, topsep=2pt, itemsep=1pt]
  \item Set $d(s)=0$;\; $d(v)=\infty$ for all other $v$.
        Mark all vertices unvisited.
  \item Pick unvisited vertex $u$ with smallest $d(u)$.
        Mark $u$ visited.
  \item For each unvisited neighbour $v$ of $u$:\\
        if $\;d(u)+w(u,v)<d(v)\;$ then $d(v)\leftarrow d(u)+w(u,v)$.
  \item Repeat steps 2--3 until all visited.
\end{enumerate}

\vspace{0.2cm}
Step 3 is called \textbf{relaxation}.
Once visited, a vertex's distance is \textbf{final}.
Trace back predecessors to reconstruct the path.

