A \textbf{tree} is a connected graph with \textbf{no cycles}.

\vspace{0.2cm}
A graph is a tree if \textbf{any one} of these holds:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.5em, itemsep=1pt]
    \item Connected and no cycles.
    \item Connected and has exactly $n-1$ edges.
    \item Any two vertices are connected by exactly one path.
    \item Connected, but removing any edge disconnects it.
\end{itemize}

\vspace{0.2cm}
A \textbf{forest} is a graph with no cycles but possibly
disconnected. Each component of a forest is a tree.

