\vspace{0.7cm}

A \textbf{binary tree} is a rooted tree where every vertex has
\textbf{at most 2 children} (called left and right child).

\vspace{0.2cm}
A \textbf{full binary tree} is a binary tree where every
internal vertex has \textbf{exactly 2 children}.

\vspace{0.2cm}
\textbf{Properties of a full binary tree:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.5em, itemsep=1pt]
    \item Leaves $=$ internal vertices $+ 1$\quad
          i.e.\ $\ell = i + 1$
    \item Total vertices $= 2i + 1$
    \item Maximum leaves at height $h$ is $2^h$
\end{itemize}

