\vspace{0.7cm}

A \textbf{BST} is a binary tree where at every node $v$:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.5em, itemsep=1pt]
    \item All keys in the \textbf{left subtree} are
          \textbf{less than} $v$.
    \item All keys in the \textbf{right subtree} are
          \textbf{greater than} $v$.
\end{itemize}

\vspace{0.2cm}
\textbf{Inserting} a key: start at root, go left if smaller,
right if larger, insert at the first empty spot.

\vspace{0.2cm}
\textbf{In-order traversal} of a BST gives keys in
\textbf{sorted ascending order}.

\vspace{0.2cm}
{\small
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|l|p{2.8cm}|p{2.8cm}|}
\hline
\rowcolor{primaryblue!20}
& \textbf{Binary Tree} & \textbf{BST} \\
\hline
Ordering & None & Left $<$ node $<$ right \\
\hline
Search & Scan all nodes & Follow comparisons \\
\hline
Use & General hierarchy & Fast search \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
}

